        "original_id": "a89a7c95-a5e8-54fa-ae32-be5e23bf1507",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: Fourier number, Fourier modulus, transient heat conduction, dimensionless number, Fourier series\n- People: Joseph Fourier\n- Fields: physics, engineering, mathematics, heat transfer, vibrations\n- Places: Auxerre\n\nFacts:\n- Jean-Baptiste Joseph Fourier was born in Auxerre on 21 March 1768 and died on 16 May 1830.\n- Joseph Fourier was a French mathematician and physicist.\n- Joseph Fourier is best known for initiating the investigation of Fourier series and their applications to heat transfer and vibrations.\n- In physics and engineering, the Fourier number, also called the Fourier modulus, is a dimensionless number named after Joseph Fourier.\n- The Fourier number characterizes transient heat conduction.",
